{
  "slug": "blackberry-clafoutis",
  "title": "Blackberry Clafoutis",
  "blurb": "A French baked pudding with blackberries suspended in a custard batter, soft in the centre with golden edges.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat your oven to 180°C and butter a shallow baking dish about 25cm across.",
    "Whisk the eggs and coconut sugar together in a large bowl until smooth.",
    "Add the flour and whisk until no lumps remain, then pour in the cream and milk and whisk to combine.",
    "Stir in the vanilla and almond extracts.",
    "Scatter the blackberries evenly over the base of the buttered dish.",
    "Pour the batter over the blackberries and transfer to the oven.",
    "Bake for 45 minutes until puffed and golden on top, with just a slight wobble in the centre when you shake the dish.",
    "Let it cool for 10 minutes before serving warm or at room temperature."
